recipient

01:08:16.521 --> 01:08:21.316
of the

01:08:21.316 --> 01:08:27.071
George

01:08:27.071 --> 01:08:34.744
GC Parker

01:08:34.744 --> 01:08:41.458
Prize is

01:08:41.458 --> 01:08:48.172
Michael

01:08:48.172 --> 01:08:56.811
Burnett.

01:08:56.811 --> 01:09:05.317
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:09:16.721 --> 01:09:19.127
&gt;&gt; Distinguished guests, faculty,

01:09:19.127 --> 01:09:21.459
staff, families, and friends.

01:09:22.580 --> 01:09:24.426
The MBA students gathered here

01:09:24.426 --> 01:09:26.272
before us today have engaged in

01:09:26.272 --> 01:09:28.890
a transformational experience.

01:09:28.890 --> 01:09:30.501
They have acquired solid

01:09:30.501 --> 01:09:32.802
foundations in general management

01:09:32.802 --> 01:09:34.872
and have pursued deeper study in

01:09:34.872 --> 01:09:36.569
their areas of interest.

01:09:36.569 --> 01:09:38.122
They have engaged in perched

01:09:38.122 --> 01:09:39.222
personal growth and

01:09:39.222 --> 01:09:40.904
built relationships that will

01:09:40.904 --> 01:09:42.200
last a lifetime.

01:09:42.200 --> 01:09:44.600
They have helped the school and

01:09:44.600 --> 01:09:47.450
community in many ways.

01:09:47.450 --> 01:09:49.196
They are an impressive group and

01:09:49.196 --> 01:09:50.877
are ready and worthy to join the

01:09:50.877 --> 01:09:52.760
ranks of our illustrious alumni.

01:09:53.760 --> 01:09:57.306
Therefore, it is my great honor and

01:09:57.306 --> 01:10:00.026
privilege to present to you

01:10:00.026 --> 01:10:03.702
the Stanford MBA Class of 2023.

01:10:03.702 --> 01:10:04.640
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:10:04.640 --> 01:10:14.640
[APPLAUSE]

01:10:24.492 --> 01:10:26.107
&gt;&gt; As you leave I hope your

01:10:26.107 --> 01:10:28.318
memories of the GSB will remain

01:10:28.318 --> 01:10:30.443
fresh, and that you will stay

01:10:30.443 --> 01:10:32.413
involved with the school.

01:10:32.413 --> 01:10:34.201
Our alumni played an important

01:10:34.201 --> 01:10:36.266
role in your academic experience,

01:10:36.266 --> 01:10:38.191
ranging from serving as judges in

01:10:38.191 --> 01:10:39.774
the executive challenge to

01:10:39.774 --> 01:10:40.943
acting as mentors in

01:10:40.943 --> 01:10:42.615
entrepreneurial courses.

01:10:42.615 --> 01:10:44.691
It is my wish that you too will

01:10:44.691 --> 01:10:47.377
engage with GSB's academic mission

01:10:47.377 --> 01:10:49.628
as alumni and give your time and

01:10:49.628 --> 01:10:52.055
experience generously to future

01:10:52.055 --> 01:10:52.850
classes.

01:10:52.850 --> 01:10:55.502
You will leave your own legacy and

01:10:55.502 --> 01:10:57.870
play a part in bringing the GSB

01:10:57.870 --> 01:11:00.809
experience to future generations as

01:11:00.809 --> 01:11:03.669
other alumni have done before you.

01:11:03.669 --> 01:11:05.951
All of you have undoubtedly heard

01:11:05.951 --> 01:11:06.930
of RJ Miller,

01:11:06.930 --> 01:11:08.803
RJ served in the US Air Force

01:11:08.803 --> 01:11:11.084
during the Second World War, and

01:11:11.084 --> 01:11:13.529
was later one of the so-called whiz

01:11:13.529 --> 01:11:15.242
kids who revolutionized

01:11:15.242 --> 01:11:16.980
the Ford Motor Company.

01:11:16.980 --> 01:11:19.685
Arjay became President of Ford, and

01:11:19.685 --> 01:11:22.391
then later, the much admired fourth

01:11:22.391 --> 01:11:25.546
Dean of the GSB from 1968 to 1978.

01:11:25.546 --> 01:11:28.305
In honor of Dean Miller's service,

01:11:28.305 --> 01:11:30.974
the top 10% of the class ranked by

01:11:30.974 --> 01:11:33.822
academic performance are designated

01:11:33.822 --> 01:11:35.607
as RJ Miller Scholars.

01:11:35.607 --> 01:11:37.220
As we read the names of

01:11:37.220 --> 01:11:39.914
the graduates we will also announce

01:11:39.914 --> 01:11:42.518
if they have achieved the academic

01:11:42.518 --> 01:11:45.229
distinction of RJ Miller Scholar.

01:11:45.229 --> 01:11:46.661
In the case of joint degree

01:11:46.661 --> 01:11:48.551
students who are walking today but

01:11:48.551 --> 01:11:50.312
not graduating we will identify

01:11:50.312 --> 01:11:52.135
those who are currently in the top

01:11:52.135 --> 01:11:53.328
10% of the class.

01:11:53.328 --> 01:11:55.408
The late Dean Miller has also

01:11:55.408 --> 01:11:57.922
founded the Certificate in Public

01:11:57.922 --> 01:12:00.436
Management and Social Innovation

01:12:00.436 --> 01:12:02.267
program here at the GSB.

01:12:02.267 --> 01:12:04.465
The certificate program educates

01:12:04.465 --> 01:12:06.589
leaders who understand societal

01:12:06.589 --> 01:12:08.104
issues, design for and

01:12:08.104 --> 01:12:10.303
evaluate impact, and understand

01:12:10.303 --> 01:12:12.653
the specificities of the management

01:12:12.653 --> 01:12:14.699
of social organizations in both

01:12:14.699 --> 01:12:16.841
the private and public sectors.

01:12:16.841 --> 01:12:20.525
This year we have 136 recipients.

01:12:20.525 --> 01:12:21.926
Their names are listed in

01:12:21.926 --> 01:12:23.533
the commencement program.

01:12:23.533 --> 01:12:30.389
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] &gt;&gt; You

01:12:30.389 --> 01:12:32.086
